# checkpoint-undo: every row rewinds and undoes through real shadow-git, ten of them through the real runner capped at
# 1500 bytes, ten under a 40-80 entry walk budget, undo review 3's over clones, a linked worktree and `.git` junctions —
# measured standalone (lane checkpoint-links): 239 s before its W rows with other gates holding the CPU at 100%, 110 s
# with them, other gates running (undo review 1, 2026-10-30); with undo review 2's rows 90 s at about 45% CPU, 98 s and
# 152 s at about 90% (2026-10-30/31); with undo review 3's 121 s and 143 s at 40-57% CPU (2026-10-31); at undo review
# 4's fix 157 s at 74% CPU (its rows went to checkpoint-undo-gitlinks, below, which keeps both under 600 s); at undo
# review 5's, no new rows, 265 s at 77% (its 126 new Git calls, the modes each rewind lists, are 6% of its 2272); undo
# review 6 measured 471 s at 86%, one row at a time (79% of the 600 s cap). Since its fix the rows run four at a time,
# each on its own agent, and no Git starts a console host, measured as checkpoint-links was (2026-11-01, after the
# reboot): 35 s at 63% CPU and 50 s at 87% beside another gate, 95 s at 99% beside another; 127 s and 133 s at 100%
# with busy threads added; 127 s and 124 s at 100% with 12-16 game instances and no gate; ab10c33's file 162 s at 75%. Before that reboot: 155 s at 62% (2026-11-01 00:21); with a
# console host beside every Git (2026-10-31), 271 s at 71% and 331 s at 86%, cut off at 600 s once at 97%. At undo review
# 7's fix (2026-11-01 evening, no new rows here): 64 s at 78% and 66 s at 87% beside two other gates, 124 s at 100% with busy
# threads added. At undo review 8's fix (2026-11-02, no new rows here): 54 s at 65% and 51 s at 53% beside another lane's
# HTTP gate; 103 s and 111 s at 94% turn about with 2caa2665's file, which took 91 s and 113 s. Undo review 9 measured
# b5355821's file at 95-97% (the three rounds below): 158 s, 194 s and 278 s. At its fix (no new rows here): 63 s at
# 55% beside another session's fast gate, and 63 s at 58% turn about with b5355821's file, which took 54 s at 53%. Undo
# review 10 measured 37ab3794's file at 74.6 s at 61% and 85.9 s at 72%; at its fix (no new rows here): 68 s at 57%. Undo review
# 11 measured d7247072's file at 96.2 s at 73%. At its fix (no new rows here, eight at a time): 156 s at 83% turn about with
# d7247072's file, which took 194 s at 82%; 166 s at 88%, and 223 s at 89% with 6 game instances and a gate beside it.
# It runs on the FAST gate since undo review 2, beside checkpoint-links: the HTTP gate (57 min deadline) took
# 46m25s-55m26s in its ten runs of 2026-10-28 to -30 and ran out of time in three. The fast gate (47 min) took
# 24m01s-37m38s in its ten runs to 2026-10-31 03:14 without the lane. Its eight since, none with a lane step, took 30m09s,
# 34m53s, 35m57s, 39m41s and 41m36s and ran out of time at 47m three times (2026-10-31 14:55 to 2026-11-02 01:16, undo
# review 9's count: the box's load, not the lane), so its slowest complete run leaves 5m24s. The lane's steps (three until
# undo review 9, four since) take more than that at 80-95% CPU (below), so a landing gate on such a box can run out of
# time: land on a quieter box, or give the landing's fast gate a longer deadline (the merge's call). The lane's three
# fast-gate steps together, 2026-11-01 after the reboot: 93 s at 54-63% CPU and 127 s at 83-88% beside another gate,
# 259 s at 96-100% beside another, 290 s at 92-100% and 318 s at 100% with busy threads added, 332 s at 99-100% with 16
# game instances and no gate, 457 s at 100% with 12-16 of them and the run queue at 45-81 (ab10c33's files 383 s at
# 61-75%); no quiet box that day. Before that reboot: 388 s at 62-70%, and undo review 6 measured ab10c33's 15m53s at 81-86%. CPU share alone
# does not say what these steps take: starting one Git held a file's main thread 43-114 ms before the reboot, 5-7 ms
# after it, even at 100%. At undo review 7's fix, with its rows in checkpoint-undo-gitlinks, that evening: 193 s and 219 s at
# 76-93% beside two other gates, 388 s at 100% with busy threads added, no step past 149 s, a quarter of its cap. At undo
# review 8's fix, its rows in checkpoint-undo-gitlinks (2026-11-02, 3a1ac507): 223 s at 50-65% and 196 s at 53-57% beside
# another lane's HTTP gate; turn about with 2caa2665's files that night, at 82-97%: 335 s and 355 s against 275 s and 325 s,
# a tenth to a fifth more, no step past 156 s, about a quarter of its cap. Undo review 9 measured b5355821's three in three
# rounds on a busier box (2026-11-02 07:43-08:51 UTC, 86-98% CPU, another lane's or another session's gate in two of them, 6-12
# game instances, 1-3 other copies of these files running): 512 s, 831 s and 994 s, checkpoint-undo-gitlinks past 300 s in the
# second and third, the three past 6 minutes in every one. At undo review 9's fix, its undo review 7 and 8 rows in
# checkpoint-undo-reads (2026-11-02 10:39-11:05 UTC): the lane's four fast-gate steps 250 s at 55-57% beside another session's
# fast gate, no step past 93 s; turn about with b5355821's three at 37-64%, another gate beside from the second step: 226 s
# against 234 s. So on a box loaded as undo review 9's was, the targets (each step at most 300 s, the lane's steps together at
# most 6 minutes) do not hold, nor does the fast gate's room: whether the landing runs on a quieter box or its fast gate gets a
# longer deadline is Andrew's call (the round-6 runtime direction); the lane leaves package.json and the workflows as they are.
# No run has timed them on Linux, where the CI fast-gate job has 30-87 s of room under its 25 minutes (undo review 9 estimates
# 15-45 s for these files there, about 4 ms a Git launch); 41 of the rows of undo reviews 7 and 8, and undo review 9's made with
# fsutil, skip where the file system does not fold case. Undo review 10 measured 37ab3794's four at 256.0 s at 46-61% and 343.9 s
# at 66-72%, beside other gates. At undo review 10's fix (2026-11-02 13:48-13:59 UTC, two other gates and 4-8 game instances
# beside them): 304 s at 55-60%, no step past 121 s; of its 14 new rows (checkpoint-undo-reads), 10 skip where the file system
# does not fold case and 4 run both calls there. The CI job's room, undo review 10's laws major, is the CI shards lane's
# (agent/ci-fast-shards-1101, in the landing queue), which splits that job into four. Undo review 11 measured d7247072's four at
# 396.4 s at 65-74% beside an HTTP gate and 4-8 game instances, no step past 153.6 s. Its fix adds 46 rows (184 in
# checkpoint-undo-reads and checkpoint-undo-case, 138 in d7247072's file), none of which runs where the file system does not fold
# case, so the CI job gets no more of them, and a Git call to each rewind there; the rows run eight at a time since. Turn about
# (2026-11-02 22:44-23:12 UTC, 2-8 game instances, a gate beside most steps), before checkpoint-undo-case was split: d7247072's
# four 785 s at 77-88%, the fix's 787 s at 83-90%; just before, at 88% both, checkpoint-undo-reads 456 s against 428 s with those rows
# in it. The fix's five, split (23:13-23:33 UTC, 6-12 game instances, a gate beside most): 1144 s at 84-94%, no step past 304 s,
# about half its cap. On such a box the 6 minutes for the lane's steps do not hold, at d7247072 as at the fix, and no run has
# timed the five at undo review 11's own 65-74%: whether the steps get a budget of their own is still Andrew's call (the round-6
# runtime direction), which undo review 11 routed there.
# At undo review 12's fix (2026-11-03 03:33-06:09 UTC, each step alone through the gate's runner, two or three other sessions' gates,
# a sweep and 2-8 game instances on the box, a lone `git --version` 77-460 ms at the median and 0.5-1.7 s at p90; no new rows here):
# 404 s at 76% with 4 game instances (04:11 UTC). The lane's nine fast-gate steps took 2,920 s together (48m40s, added from runs
# between 03:33 and 05:39 UTC), the longest checkpoint-undo-older's 492 s, 82% of its cap.
# Turn about at that load, 551bca25's checkpoint-undo-gitlinks took 194 s and 336 s run directly and the fix's 366 s, the same
# 1,719 Git launches each time (p50 416 ms and 461 ms a launch, p95 2.7-2.9 s): what these steps take on such a box is the box's, not
# the store's, and neither the 300 s a step nor the 6 minutes for the lane's steps holds there. checkpoint-undo-case,
# checkpoint-undo-reads and checkpoint-links were split at that fix (undo review 12's laws MAJOR), so at the load that review measured
# them (case 396.7-476.8 s, reads 318.4 s, links 208.9 s, at 80-99%) each step holds about half of what one did; whether the lane's
# steps get a budget of their own stays Andrew's call (the round-6 runtime direction), as undo reviews 11 and 12 routed it.
test/checkpoint-undo.test.js
